  "originalQuery": "You are managing a data analytics project where daily logs of around 10 TB are generated on-premises. This data needs to be transferred securely and efficiently to Google Cloud Storage for further analysis in BigQuery. Your solution must ensure the transfer is completed in a timely manner with the least amount of manual intervention. What should you do?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Set up a cron job on an on-premises server to perform daily uploads to Cloud Storage using gsutil.<br/>B. Utilize Transfer Appliance to send data to Google Cloud Storage daily.<br/>C. Employ Storage Transfer Service to schedule daily data synchronization from on-premises to Cloud Storage.<br/>D. Configure a Dataflow template to extract data from on-premises and load it into Cloud Storage every day.",
